REM ============================================================
REM  04 - TIMING: THE #1 CAUSE OF BROKEN PAYLOADS
REM  DuckyScript 1.0  ->  Pico Duck OK
REM
REM  A duck types at hardware speed. Windows is not ready for it.
REM  Every "my payload stops halfway" bug is usually a missing DELAY.
REM ============================================================

REM DEFAULT_DELAY applies to every keystroke that follows.
REM 0 = as fast as USB allows (great for shells, terrible for UIs).
DEFAULT_DELAY 0
REM Type this fast into Notepad and characters WILL be dropped on
REM a busy machine. Watch it happen, then fix it below.

GUI r
DELAY 700                REM Run dialog needs time to appear
STRING notepad
ENTER
DELAY 1500               REM Notepad needs time to draw

REM Now slow down for UI work. 50 ms is a good default for typing.
DEFAULT_DELAY 50
STRING This is typed at 50 ms per keystroke - reliable in most UIs.
ENTER

REM For anything that renders slowly (browsers, Electron apps,
REM first launch after boot) use a one-off DELAY instead:
DELAY 2000

REM --- rules of thumb ---
REM   after GUI r ..................... 700-1000 ms
REM   after launching an app .......... 1200-2500 ms
REM   between menu interactions ....... 300-600 ms
REM   typing into a UI ................ DEFAULT_DELAY 50
REM   typing into a console ........... DEFAULT_DELAY 0-10
REM
REM On a cold boot add 3-5 seconds at the very top of the payload.
REM In a VM add more: virtualised USB is slower than real hardware.

DELAY 500
STRINGLN Timing demo finished.
